00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:00.550 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  baber and mid-suffolk district councils  both declared a climate and biodiversity  emergency in 2019  since then we've worked with our suffolk  climate change partnership colleagues to  approve our first carbon reduction  management plan and biodiversity action  plan  these plans set out how we aim to  achieve our ambition to become carbon  neutral by 2030  and how we'll improve and strengthen our  district's plant life and wildlife  our work so far has included becoming  the first rural uk councils to move our  fleet to hydro-treated vegetable oil  a change which will reduce our total co2  emissions by a quarter and reduce our  fleet emissions by up to 90 percent  securing 3.6 million pounds in  government funding to make our homes  more energy efficient and add energy  saving measures and trial solar carport  technology at our leisure centers  supporting our communities with grants  and advice for new green projects such  as electric vehicle charging points  giving out equipment and supporting  hundreds of litter-picking groups to  help keep the districts clean and tidy  working with our suffolk waste  partnership colleagues to help increase  and improve the quality of recycling  across suffolk  but we know there's still more to do and  ways we can support our residents to  reduce their carbon emissions too  find out more and keep up to date with  our progress at  www.greensuffolk.org forward slash news

